{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/494480-2nd-edition-and-spirit-claimed-information","id":494480,"title":"2nd Edition and Spirit/Claimed Information","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-28T00:32:07-07:00","id":494480,"title":"2nd Edition and Spirit/Claimed Information","content":"While it seems a sure thing that the werewolf book would have more information on spirits than GMC, does it have more information on the Claimed?<br /> <br /> Also, how would a claimed play as compared to a full template supernatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T04:09:52-07:00","id":496172,"title":"","content":"There are a few example Claimed in the Prey section of the Werewolf book, but the information about them as a group is very similar to what's in the GMC. The main difference is that instead of saying they can develop Supernatural Merits, it says they can develop Dread Powers. It does not give a specific system for doing this, though, as they are not meant to be player characters.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to play a person who's consciousness has been shunted aside by a spirit, then a) role-playing would be very weird, b) you wouldn't have a power stat (such as Primal Urge or Wyrd or Psyche) and c) you wouldn't have any special powers other than a couple dots of Influence and the possibility of picking up Dread Powers along the way somehow. You'd have super-jacked stats, but overall I think they're better off as antagonist NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:42:29-07:00","id":496199,"title":"","content":"Until we get expanded information about them you're better off using the Predators book if you want them as some sort of player character.<br /> <br /> For antagonist NPCs, the second edition should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:42:44-07:00","id":496200,"title":"","content":"A claimed's human consciousness isn't shunted aside so much as merged with the spirit. <br /> <br /> Anyway, if you wanted to play as a claimed you'd probably need to 1) assign dot ratings to the non-rated dread powers (predators in 1st edition did this so that might give you a decent guideline) and 2) come up with some metric to determine how many dots a character could possess, such as 5 dots per rank or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:40:23-07:00","id":496383,"title":"","content":"One other thing said about the Claimed in WtF 2E is in the Iminir's Steryotypes sidebar: They consider Sin-Eaters among the claimed. You can play as a Sin-Eater without any trouble, but Geist would be the book to buy for that, not WtF 2E","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:26:34-07:00","id":496593,"title":"","content":"The Claimed &amp; Dread Powers in WtF 2e are designed for use as a Storyteller's toolbox, hence why the lack of dot ratings based on 'power level' for the different entries etc. For the WtF Dread Powers, the dots serve as a quick-reference numerical guide on certain entries to inform you of what effect the creature has with that particular power, rather than being used as any sort of balancing system or measure. Claimed can explicitly have as many Dread Powers as are needed for them to work as the Storyteller desires.<br /> <br /> This does mean it's not massively useful for building a Claimed character to play; Werewolf pitches the Claimed very much as prey and Storyteller characters, not as a playable aspect of the game. That doesn't mean you shouldn't do it in your own games, but it does mean the new core doesn't provide a massive amount of support for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I'd be interested to see how someone's attempt to roleplay a Hive-Claimed would turn out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I actually had more explicit, detailed rules for how Hive-Claimed worked and should be roleplayed but sadly had to cut it down to a more manageable length for the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:26:36-07:00","id":496695,"title":"","content":"Damn manageable lengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:39:23-07:00","id":496830,"title":"","content":"Thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:30:47-07:00","id":496894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/494480-2nd-edition-and-spirit-claimed-information?p=496593#post496593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I actually had more explicit, detailed rules for how Hive-Claimed worked and should be roleplayed but sadly had to cut it down to a more manageable length for the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance you could ask Rich and Stew about posting those here? I'd understand if they want to save them for a supplement, but if they don't have a plan for that, forum posts don't need to be a manageable length.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:16:43-07:00","id":497030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/494480-2nd-edition-and-spirit-claimed-information?p=496172#post496172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> b) you wouldn't have a power stat (such as Primal Urge or Wyrd or Psyche) and c) you wouldn't have any special powers other than a couple dots of Influence and the possibility of picking up Dread Powers along the way somehow. You'd have super-jacked stats, but overall I think they're better off as antagonist NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have their rank as a power stat. Additionally...<br /> <br /> Powers<br /> -Influence(s)<br /> -Dread Powers (Assuming the player and the story teller arrive at appropriate dots and costs)<br /> -Essence buffing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:13:19-07:00","id":497095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A claimed's human consciousness isn't shunted aside so much as merged with the spirit. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One other thing said about the Claimed in WtF 2E is in the Iminir's Steryotypes sidebar: They consider Sin-Eaters among the claimed. </div> </div> </div>That is amazing! ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also an aside, there is mention in certain Gifts, the Wisdom Facet Nature and Technology Gifts infact, of an Uratha warging into an animal or a machine and potentially due to incident becoming some kind of unnatural Claimed with these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:01:46-07:00","id":497295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/494480-2nd-edition-and-spirit-claimed-information?p=496894#post496894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any chance you could ask Rich and Stew about posting those here? I'd understand if they want to save them for a supplement, but if they don't have a plan for that, forum posts don't need to be a manageable length.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess that if we would get a new book that describes the prey of werewolves, it would have a place there.<br /> <br /> It just hit me that under the new paradigm, the book &quot;Predators&quot; should actually be called &quot;Prey&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}